course: dictionary
lesson: 5248
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word jock is a good example. Read the words around it before you decide.
explain: «British road signs were designed by Jock Kinneir and Margaret Calvert.» Here Jock is a person's first name, not a sporty boy. The clues are the names, Kinneir and Calvert, and the work of designing road signs.
explain: In American school stories, a jock is a sporty, popular boy. Stories often show that people are more than their label, so a word like this can be unfair when it is used to judge someone.
explain: In the UK, Jock can be a friendly nickname for a Scottish friend, but it can be rude when a stranger uses it. Always think about who is speaking and how they say it.
fact: A jock is a noun: one jock, two jocks.
fact: In American school stories, a jock is a sporty, popular young person, especially a boy.
fact: Jock can be short for a DJ (disc jockey), who plays music on the radio, or a jockey, who rides racehorses.
fact: Jock is also a name for a Scottish man, and it can be rude if a stranger uses it.
fact: A stereotype is a fixed idea about a whole group, such as «dumb jock», which is a rude stereotype.
exercise: «British road signs were designed by Jock Kinneir and Margaret Calvert.» In this sentence, what is Jock? | A sporty boy at school | *A person's first name | A radio DJ | A horse
exercise: In American school stories, what is a jock? | A horse that wins races | A kind of road sign | *A sporty, popular young person | A teacher who gives lots of homework
exercise: A «radio jock» plays music on the radio. What does jock mean in this phrase? | A kind of sport | A Scottish man | A person who writes books | *Short for disc jockey, a DJ
test: Why is «dumb jock» an unfair label? | It means a very clever sports star | It is the name of a famous racehorse | It describes a road sign | *It is a rude stereotype that judges people by one label
test: A friend calls his Scottish mate «Jock» and they both laugh. What does it mean here? | Road sign | *A friendly nickname | Horse | Radio show
exam: Which clue shows that «Jock» in the road sign sentence is a name? | *The names Kinneir and Calvert, and the sentence about designing | The word British | The word sign on its own | The word drivers
